    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "RAY COOKE AUCTIONEERS proudly present this three bedroom semi-detached bungalow to the market tucked away towards the end of a Cul-de-sac within this highly sought after development. \r\n\r\nCherrywood Grove continues to be in high demand and will be equally sought after based on the mature and established surroundings. Within walking distance you will find Corkagh Park, Clondalkin Village and a host of shops, schools and leisure facilities, not to mention the M50 Motorway and The Luas all within a couple of minutes' drive. \r\n\r\nInterior living accommodation of c. 71 Sqm comprises of entrance hallway, lounge, kitchen/breakfast, three bedrooms and the family bathroom. Externally this property benefits from a South/West facing low maintenance rear garden with patio area, brick built storage shed and side access that leads to the front which benefits from a gated driveway for off road parking. No.65 comes to the market in good condition throughout and offers a long list of benefits including double glazed windows, gas central heating and no forward chain. \r\n\r\nBased on location, scope and type of property we know this will be extremely popular so please contact Ray Cooke Auctioneers to register your interest. \r\n\r\nKey Features\r\nBER D\r\nC. Sqm 71\r\nSOUTH/WEST facing garden\r\nNo onward chain\r\nThree bedrooms\r\nHighly sought after development\r\nEasy access to N7 & M50\r\nGas central heating\r\nClose to Clondalkin Village\r\nGated driveway to front\r\nClose to all local amenities\r\n\r\nDirections\r\nFrom Clondalkin Village, head east on Main Street, continue onto Boot Road, turn left onto Neilstown Road, then left again onto Ninth Lock Road, take the first exit at the roundabout onto Monastery Road, turn right onto Cherrywood Drive, and follow it until you reach 65 Cherrywood Grove on your left."
      },
      {
